  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "7b3c7445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 0,
      "content": "General CSUSM Information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "31e37145-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "THE ARTICULATION AGREEMENT BELOW IS SUBJECT TO PERIODIC REVISION. PLEASE CONSULT A COUNSELOR EVERY SEMESTER TO OBTAIN CURRENT INFORMATION ABOUT POSSIBLE CHANGES IN THE AGREEMENT. Admissions and Transfer Information Academic Advising It is recommended students meet with an advisor each semester. Minimum Grade of C All courses counted toward the major, including preparation for the major courses, must be completed with a letter grade of C (2.0) or better. Credit/No Credit grading is not accepted. Language Proficiency Requirement For some majors, students must meet a second-language proficiency requirement. This is satisfied with the first semester of an intermediate language or demonstrating proficiency in a language other than English. For details on how to satisfy this requirement, please refer to Language Proficiency Requirement.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>THE ARTICULATION AGREEMENT BELOW IS SUBJECT TO PERIODIC REVISION. PLEASE CONSULT A COUNSELOR EVERY SEMESTER TO OBTAIN CURRENT INFORMATION ABOUT POSSIBLE CHANGES IN THE AGREEMENT.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><a href=\"https://www.csusm.edu/admissions/how-to-apply/transfer/index.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Admissions and Transfer Information</a></p><p><br></p><p><a href=\"https://www.csusm.edu/academicadvising/index.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic Advising</a></p><p>It is recommended students meet with an advisor each semester.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Minimum Grade of C</u></strong></p><p>All courses counted toward the major, including preparation for the major courses, must be completed with a letter grade of C (2.0) or better. Credit/No Credit grading is not accepted.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Language Proficiency Requirement</u></strong></p><p>For some majors, students must meet a second-language proficiency requirement. This is satisfied with the first semester of an intermediate language or demonstrating proficiency in a language other than English. For details on how to satisfy this requirement, please refer to <a href=\"https://catalog.csusm.edu/content.php?catoid=11&amp;navoid=2003\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Language Proficiency Requirement.</a></p>"
    },
